## STANDING LINES
1. **PRIOR-WORK CHECK, before you edit.** In your clone: `git log --oneline -n 8 d8981b0e -- api/src/HpsmPoc.Modules.Reporting/Narrative api/tests/HpsmPoc.Modules.Reporting.Tests/Narrative` (expected newest `9eeabb7c`, the grouped-summary change); `git log -S'findings share this action' --oneline d8981b0e -- api` (expected `9eeabb7c`; positive control; zero control `-S'zzz-no-such-b1060'` nothing); `git log -S'GroupSizes' --oneline d8981b0e -- api`. Jira, reads only, every JQL `project = HPSMPOC AND ( ... )`: `text ~ "GroupSizes"`, `text ~ "share this action"`, `text ~ "NarrativeOutputValidator"` (say which keys are about this guard; positive control: the ticket's own key). Read as claims: `Briefs/2026-10-22_B477_STATUS.md` lines 145-160, 318-345, 361-367; the B488 gate STATUS if it exists (`ls Briefs/*B488*`). **Prior work is NOT redone and NOT undone:** the grouped summary (#186), its goldens and its ruled words stay. **A READY FOR QA without a PRIOR WORK section is returned unread.**
2. **PHASE SCOPE.** As the fourth paragraph. Nothing in this lane connects to a device, fleet, firmware, SIEM or Security Manager tool.
3. **No production, no demo or UAT deploy, no hosted site, no HTTP to any hosted host, no `az`, no Kudu, no docker, no ssh session.** Network: `dotnet restore` (NuGet), the one `git fetch` and the one `git push`, `gh` (`-X GET`) only.
4. **No message to any human.** No mail, chat or PR comment; you never open, merge, edit or comment on a PR and never write Jira. No person's name in STATUS, code, test names or the commit message (say "the product owner"). No decision-card id, `C-` entry number, ticket key, `B###` or `B477` in changed lines or the message. No Artifact, Docs, publish, decision-queue or scoreboard tool.
5. **WORDS.** No customer-visible string changes (see the bold paragraph at the top and D-3). Exception and log text unchanged. Test names are plain ASCII and name the rule.
6. **Never skip a failure.** Fix the root cause and re-verify end to end; never `Skip`, retry-to-green, sleep-for-timing or environment-gate a row. **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -d/-D`, `--prune`, `update-ref -d`, `worktree prune`, `gc`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `checkout -- <file>`); quarantine to `.tools/b1060/_quarantine/`. A planted file is restored by `cp` from the committed blob. The one removal allowed is your own `heavy.lock`.
7. **Shell:** never type `cd` (a hook refuses it); absolute single-quoted paths (they contain `!`); `git -C`; `git --no-optional-locks` for read verbs; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `${VAR}:path` (zsh reads `$H:w...` as a modifier); heredocs QUOTED; `bash` for arrays and `PIPESTATUS`; python only as `python3 -I -B`; no unquoted word starting with `=`. **Every count printed in STATUS is printed by the command that makes it.** Stop every process you start; kill only by pid plus cwd.
8. **Locks and heartbeats.** `lock.sh` (copied, `cmp`) wraps git REF WRITES and the fetch/push on the shared `.tools/.git-lock`; it exits 99 after 10 minutes: write `.tools/.git-lock`'s mtime into STATUS and end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <is .tools/.git-lock stale>`. Heavy jobs (restore, build, every `dotnet test`, the plants) take the seat-local `.tools/b1060/heavy.lock`: make `heavy.sh` from `lock.sh` changing ONLY the `L=` line (print the `diff`); copy `waitload.sh` from `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/HPSM-POC/.tools/b267/` (`cmp`) and make `waitload7.sh` changing ONLY the threshold (below 7), printing the `diff`. Heavy runs only while load1 is below 7, two reads about 4 s apart (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER: load1 7.49 at 21:57, so expect a wait). One `dotnet test` at a time. Every waiter prints a heartbeat figure that MOVES at least every 30 s into `.tools/b1060/logs/heartbeat.txt`; frozen for 3 beats = stuck: say so.
9. **STATUS-NOW (binding).** At Step 0, before any heavy work, write `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/HPSM-POC/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-01_B1060_STATUS.md` holding: a placeholder FIRST line `PROGRESS B1060: b1060/reporting-grouped-summary-guard PENDING`; Step 0 (the brief copied unchanged into `Briefs/`, `cmp`, both sha256s, the slot count with its control, the REFUSE counts, `gh auth status`, the `brief_seat: model=...` line or "not visible", the Step-0 `date`, the absolute target READY and HARD STOP clocks); PINS; one line per step 2 to 12; and a **`WORKING:` line as the LAST line, updated after every part**. Check STATUS for non-ASCII after each write. **Do NOT write `READY FOR QA:`, `STOPPED:` or `BLOCKED:` as the last line until you mean it (a watcher fires on those).** At about 80% of context, rewrite a `## PROGRESS and RESUME` section (per step: done / partial / not started, evidence paths, the exact next commands, every scratch tree with its restore proof, processes still running, the branch state by `gh api`) before any further heavy step; if READY is not reachable before 88%, stop every process and end the FILE with exactly `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?`.
